        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "0.1 mmol (21.2 mg) 2-amino-1,2-diphenylethanol, 0.2 mmol (31.3 mg) o-vanillin, and 0.2 mmol (87.7 mg) Dy(NO3)3·5H2O were added to a ~25 cm Pyrex tube, then 0.5 mL anhydrous methanol was added and the mixture was shaken until dissolved. 30 μL Et3N was added, followed by 1.0 mL methanol and 0.5 mL acetonitrile (total 2 mL mixed solvent, VMeOH:VMeCN = 1.5:0.5). The tube was sealed and heated solvothermally at 80 °C for 48 h, then wrapped in a cotton blanket and slowly cooled to room temperature, giving yellow crystals of cluster 1 on the tube wall.",
